flowchart TB
accTitle: Planning branches do not commit to the current simulated world
accDescr: A versioned root snapshot seeds a planning state. Candidate commands are applied to isolated branch snapshots through the deterministic simulator. Candidate branches are replayed and evaluated. A separate later grounding path changes the current world only after required authorization and dispatch.

    ROOT[Root snapshot<br/>version v]
    ROOT --> S0[Planning root state]
    S0 --> C1[Candidate action A]
    S0 --> C2[Candidate action B]
    C1 --> SIM1[Simulator transition<br/>isolated branch]
    C2 --> SIM2[Simulator transition<br/>isolated branch]
    SIM1 --> E1[Replay and evaluate]
    SIM2 --> E2[Replay and evaluate]
    E1 --> CAND[Auditable plan candidate]
    E2 --> CAND
    CAND --> AUTH[Later authorization<br/>and dispatch]
    AUTH --> WORLD[Current simulated world<br/>may advance]
